{{Term/Store|Dinraal's Claw|Dinraal's Claws|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Dinraal's Claw}}<br/>This valuable claw was plucked from the red spirit Dinraal. It was extremely hot before it was removed. You could sell it to a store, but it must have some other use.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Dinraal's Claw}}<br/>This valuable claw is said to have once been covered in flames. Attach it to a weapon to greatly increase its attack power. It can also be cooked or sold.|Inventory|TotK}}</ref>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Dinraal's Claws can be collected from the [[Dragon]] [[Dinraal]], who typically flies around the [[Eldin Mountains]] and the [[Tabantha Frontier]]. [[Link]] must shoot its hands with an [[Arrow]]. The Claws in question will fall onto the land in the form of light.

Dinraal's Claws that are used in a [[Cooking Pot]] will make [[Dubious Food]]. However, when used with critters, the result will be [[Elixir]]s. At the [[Kochi Dye Shop]], Dinraal's Claws are one of the ingredients that can be used to make [[Crimson Dye]]. They also count as [[Monster Part]]s, which means they can be exchanged for [[Mon]] at the [[Fang and Bone]].

Dinraal's Claws are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Dinraal's Claw}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}

Dinraal's Claws are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Dinraal's Claw}}
In addition, one Dinraal's Claw is required to complete the [[Goddess Statue of Power]] [[Side Quest]].

